ments used for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTimeOnly":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTimeOnly","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTimeOnly"}],"type":"topic","title":"MXLTimeOnly","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltimeonly","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The time-only type is used to indicate that a particular playback- or listening-related element only applies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"particular times through a repeated section. The value is a list of positive integers arranged in ascending"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, indicating which times through the repeated section that the element applies."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTimeOnly"}]}